---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT, DELETION, LEGAL_UPDATED } from "../site";
---

<Base title="Terms · Tempra" description="The terms for using Tempra during its private beta.">
  <article class="legal" aria-labelledby="title">
    <header class="doc-head">
      <h1 id="title" class="doc-title">Terms</h1>
      <p class="doc-tagline">Last updated <time datetime={LEGAL_UPDATED.iso}>{LEGAL_UPDATED.text}</time></p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        These terms cover Tempra at tempra.dev, the landing page and the app. By using Tempra you agree to
        them. Questions go to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. The service</h2>
      <p>
        Tempra is in private beta and experimental. It may change, pause or end, and these terms may
        change with it; we will date each change here.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Your account</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Keep your email account and the tokens you create safe.</li>
        <li>
          You are responsible for what is done with your account, including by the agents and apps
          you connect to it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Your content</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You own your content. We store and serve it only to run the service.</li>
        <li>
          People you share a library with can read it, comment on it and, if you let them, change it.
        </li>
        <li>
          If @tempra is turned on for a library's owner, it reads that library to answer comments,
          as the <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> page explains.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Use Tempra for your own knowledge and your agents. Do not store anything illegal, or other
          people's private data without their consent.
        </li>
        <li>Do not try to break, overload or get around the service's limits or security.</li>
        <li>
          Do not pose as someone else, Tempra, or its staff. We may rename or reclaim a handle that
          does, or that holds a name for no use.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Limits and suspension</h2>
      <p>
        Limits apply to libraries, tokens, storage and requests. We may suspend an account that
        abuses the service or breaks these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Ending</h2>
      <p>
        You can delete a library or your account at any time from the app. {DELETION} Keep your own
        exports.
      </p>

      <h2>7. No warranty</h2>
      <p>The service is provided as is, with no warranty.</p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
